# Milestone: v0.10.2-reactive (W6)
# Covers: sleep(duration) inside an every() body strand does not crash.
#
# every() spawns a body strand per period.  If the body calls sleep(),
# the body strand parks on the sleep queue.  The body+sleep cadence
# (spec §11.4) means the periodic's current_strand pointer is held while
# the body sleeps.  urbi_periodic_body_completed fires after the body strand
# resumes from sleep and reaches OP_RET — not while it is sleeping.
# The periodic only re-arms after the body (including its sleep) finishes.
#
# PASS criteria: every(1us) body that calls sleep(1us) completes without
# crashing; subsequent reads are valid.

# Install every() that calls sleep inside its body.
Realm.done = 0
every (1us) sleep(1us)
0
0
true
[00000000] 0
[00000001] nil
[00000002] 0
[00000003] 0
[00000004] true
